<p>Taiwan President Lai Ching-te canceled a planned five-day trip to Eswatini after Madagascar, Mauritius, and Seychelles denied or revoked overflight clearance for his aircraft, according to reported accounts from Taiwan and the African governments involved. Lai had been scheduled to leave on 2026-04-22 to attend celebrations marking the 40th anniversary of King Mswati III’s accession and his 58th birthday in Eswatini, the only African country that maintains diplomatic ties with Taiwan. Taiwan said the denials reflected pressure from Beijing. China, in turn, praised the decisions and said the African countries were upholding the one-China principle, while denying it had coerced them.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/u3P5iJ4BPo7FBxJkFfCPYUaZ25dgEi5ckG4IJXpkn93KVzn0SI3DdZm8JBlxVGZheYKdTk4CdjMbsl5uERPclVhXsRGXW54EU_A1a2tOCRcEWAn0nWhfNbvZsXc9gSyhi__olVDwTEi3c_MvTPUaGCz6xblCbyiBiIMgXDgmPyFc2CdoT4Avrt34m2SvTRb0uy1bqvW7yKBMtnKjCnVCUJTBptJcrs9dyiIn38c4L7RVr8I4lpQSCM6MQxcxLg4bIwAipGR8AHCROh-0idiyQBs' alt='Taiwan President Lai Ching-te in a file photo tied to coverage of the canceled Eswatini trip.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Planned itinerary: Lai’s office said the trip was set to begin Wednesday and last five days, focused on royal celebrations in Eswatini rather than a broader African tour.</li><li>Denied route: Madagascar’s foreign ministry confirmed it rejected the overflight request, while reports said Mauritius and Seychelles also refused permission for the aircraft to pass through their airspace.</li><li>Beijing’s message: China publicly welcomed the three countries’ decisions as support for the one-China principle and opposition to what it calls Taiwan separatist activities.</li><li>A rare diplomatic tie: Eswatini remains Taiwan’s only diplomatic partner in Africa, giving the canceled visit unusual symbolic weight for Taipei’s remaining formal alliances on the continent.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Taiwan government: Taiwan blamed the flight permit denials on Chinese pressure and cast the cancellations as part of Beijing’s broader effort to restrict the international movements of Taiwan’s president. (<a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/china/taiwan-president-cancels-eswatini-trip-blames-chinese-pressure-african-countries-2026-04-21/'>Reuters</a>)</li><li>Chinese government: Beijing denied pressuring the African states and said their actions showed support for the one-China principle. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/china-hails-countries-for-blocking-taiwan-president-s-flight/a-76891296'>DW</a>)</li><li>African governments: Madagascar’s foreign ministry said plainly that it had denied the overflight request. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/taiwan-president-cancels-africa-trip-blaming-chinese-pressure/article70888985.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>SCMP analysis: The episode was presented as a sign of Beijing’s growing influence in Africa, where most governments already recognize China rather than Taiwan. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/politics/article/3351028/does-william-lais-cancelled-eswatini-trip-show-beijings-reach-africa'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/politics/article/3351028/does-william-lais-cancelled-eswatini-trip-show-beijings-reach-africa'>Does William Lai’s cancelled eSwatini trip show Beijing’s reach in Africa?</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/taiwan-president-cancels-africa-trip-blaming-chinese-pressure/article70888985.ece'>Taiwan president cancels Africa trip blaming Chinese pressure</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/china-hails-countries-for-blocking-taiwan-president-s-flight/a-76891296'>China hails countries for blocking Taiwan president&#x27;s flight</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crl16p72x7xo'>Taiwan president cancels trip after African countries revoke flight permits</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/china/taiwan-president-cancels-eswatini-trip-blames-chinese-pressure-african-countries-2026-04-21/'>Taiwanese president Lai Ching-te cancels his planned visit to Eswatini after the governments of Madagascar, Mauritius, and Seychelles denied overflight permissions for his aircraft, with Taiwan attributing the decision to pressure from China.</a> - reuters.com</li></ul>